		{
			"id": "trynAg1MAlWNq5wIF",
			"name": "Haemonculus Regrowth",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "One Extra Life. On death, if a fragment reaches a Coven and the price is met, the character is regrown and returns, changed a little (GM's choice of small physical or mental side effect).\n\nLore: Haemonculi can regrow the dead from little more than a scrap, and the Covens sell that service to the powerful. Archons and their favoured servants are the ones who can afford the price, in coin, slaves or service. Codex: Drukhari background.\n\nDesign: Extra Life (B55, 25 points) with Accessibility (B110) -40% for the recovered-fragment and coven-fee requirements. 25 x 0.6 = 15 points. Reserved for Archons, favoured servants and Haemonculi; ordinary Kabalites and Wyches do not have it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "m9YrT_QlkN-zDe1wb",
					"name": "Accessibility",
					"reference": "B110",
					"local_notes": "Needs a body fragment (at least the head or a torso) recovered to a Haemonculus and a Coven paid for the work; lasts one life.",
					"cost_adj": "-40%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 25
		},
		{
			"id": "TliaSOLIBYfPDV4ME",
			"name": "Power from Pain",
			"local_notes": "Lore: All three stages together: the full Power from Pain a Drukhari of rank earns in a long fight.\n\nDesign: 7 + 7 + 20 = 34 points. Lower-tier templates include the single stages above instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tqqHnCH-WTMiQw_Dm",
					"name": "Power from Pain (Stage I)",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "High Pain Threshold, once feeding has begun. Stage I of three; each later stage needs the one before it. A stage lapses at the end of the scene.\n\nLore: Every Drukhari fights harder for the taste of blood. Codex background describes the Dark Eldar as growing bolder and stronger as the killing goes on, feeding on the pain they cause; the exact stages differ between Kabals, Wych Cults and Covens.\n\nDesign: High Pain Threshold (B59, 10 points) with Accessibility (B110) -30% for its trigger: 10 x 0.7 = 7 points. Deliberately no `attributes` feature: the bonus is conditional and must not raise the sheet's stats before the trigger.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mBVE_7Jh3ZqaMc_fr",
							"name": "Accessibility",
							"reference": "B110",
							"local_notes": "Only after the Drukhari, or a comrade in the same unit, has drawn blood or caused real suffering in this scene.",
							"cost_adj": "-30%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "TycDZTZNDcArw90-j",
					"name": "Power from Pain (Stage II)",
					"local_notes": "Stage II: melee and Fright Check bonuses (requires Stage I), lapses at the end of the scene.\n\nLore: By the time a fight has really turned, a Drukhari hits harder and cannot be frightened. Background: the Power from Pain rule in Codex: Drukhari (per unit, by kills scored).\n\nDesign: Melee and morale bonuses only; the real weight is small (5 + 2 = 7 points). Not `attributes`: the bonuses are conditional.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tlgNLKPzALD9kEOsw",
							"name": "Bloodied Strength",
							"reference": "B88",
							"local_notes": "Striking ST +2: melee damage as if ST 2 higher.\n\nLore: The Kabalite's cruelty in melee sharpens as the blood flows.\n\nDesign: Striking ST 2 (B88, 5/level, 10) with Accessibility -50% = 5 points.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Physical",
								"Xenos",
								"Drukhari"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mv8zTqDiOgRKlZgQk",
									"name": "Accessibility",
									"reference": "B110",
									"local_notes": "Only after Stage I plus at least one enemy dropped or seriously hurt in this scene by the Drukhari's unit.",
									"cost_adj": "-50%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 2
						},
						{
							"id": "t5rpqWUD7mqR6yV52",
							"name": "Bloodied Nerve",
							"reference": "B55",
							"local_notes": "Fearlessness +2 to Fright Checks.\n\nLore: A feeding Drukhari does not flinch from the things that break other people.\n\nDesign: Fearlessness 2 (B55, 2/level, 4) with Accessibility -50% = 2 points.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Drukhari"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mq0eTLWLIMdfCsLM4",
									"name": "Accessibility",
									"reference": "B110",
									"local_notes": "Same trigger as Bloodied Strength.",
									"cost_adj": "-50%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 2,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tDH_POtd__V5We2Nc",
					"name": "Power from Pain (Stage III)",
					"reference": "B80",
					"local_notes": "Regeneration (Fast): 1 HP per minute (roughly 1 HP per 6 combat turns of 10 seconds when tracking turns).\n\nLore: The height of the feed: wounds close as fast as the killer can reopen new ones in other people. Codex: Drukhari's third stage is the strongest bonus a unit can earn.\n\nDesign: Regeneration, Fast tier (B80, 50 points, 1 HP per minute) with Accessibility -60%: 50 x 0.4 = 20 points. Kept at Fast rather than faster because the lore effect is 'hard to put down', not 'cannot be killed'.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Drukhari"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m-XUnR7Jkw4-Sn5Ts",
							"name": "Accessibility",
							"reference": "B110",
							"local_notes": "Only after Stages I and II and at least three enemies dropped or badly hurt in this scene by the Drukhari's unit.",
							"cost_adj": "-60%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 50
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tjd3gUas9n-63-6qV",
			"name": "Sadism",
			"reference": "B152",
			"local_notes": "Takes pleasure in others' suffering and seeks chances to inflict it; roll self-control when the chance arises.\n\nLore: Cruelty is Commorragh's native culture, not a deviance. Most Drukhari, and every Haemonculus, take an openly aesthetic interest in others' pain (Codex: Drukhari and background across editions). The self-control 12 default represents someone who can hold off when it would cost them, e.g. in front of a superior.\n\nDesign: Sadism (B152, -15) with self-control 12.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -15,
			"cr": 12
		},
		{
			"id": "tLIi8_3zdCvpoepbg",
			"name": "Callous",
			"reference": "B125",
			"local_notes": "Indifferent to others' pain; -3 reaction when it shows.\n\nLore: Even a Drukhari who does not enjoy suffering treats it as currency. Background.\n\nDesign: Callous (B125, -5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tDDt-I1v6sXuHw-PT",
			"name": "Obsession (Perfect Agony)",
			"reference": "B146",
			"local_notes": "Consumed by a lifelong artistic project (a perfect pain, a perfect body); self-control roll to abandon a chance to advance it.\n\nLore: Every Haemonculus is driven by an aesthetic quest no one else understands. Background.\n\nDesign: Obsession (B146, -10) for a long-term goal.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"base_points": -10,
			"cr": 12
		}
	],
